                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d480ef9-156d-3672-b069-6e2e105e410c",
                        "entry_id": "8d2248f5-d315-3668-b6c3-5f00a437e35d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Interrogatif, qui cherche à obtenir une information en parlant d’un énoncé ou d’un mot, souvent d’un connecteur logique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e760cc90-7552-4bc3-b4ec-dbb5644ca951",
                                "sense_id": "1d480ef9-156d-3672-b069-6e2e105e410c",
                                "text": "L’énoncé est percontatif (du latin Percontari : « s’informer, questionner »). Le locuteur cherche à obtenir des informations de la part de son interlocuteur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1088b23-bd9e-4e0d-8f88-ea4b432c8033",
                                "sense_id": "1d480ef9-156d-3672-b069-6e2e105e410c",
                                "text": "Destinés à l’usage interne, ces quatre mots provoquèrent néanmoins la réponse que voici : qu’est-ce qui n’en fait pas. Avec un point d’interrogation, car la réponse était percontative."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "682b55c9-5dc9-428e-a18e-3b65f04b244a",
                        "source_entry_id": "8d2248f5-d315-3668-b6c3-5f00a437e35d",
                        "source_sense_id": "1d480ef9-156d-3672-b069-6e2e105e410c",
                        "target_lang_word": "percontative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "percontative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b0a5cf0-449d-31c9-9859-f06e10192134",
                                        "entry_id": "540dd832-21a2-3a61-b7bf-477b102e0fd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That is, expressed in, or having the character of the grammatical mood (mode) of rhetorical questioning; percontatorial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2757714b-6860-4252-834b-254222a4cec8",
                                                "sense_id": "3b0a5cf0-449d-31c9-9859-f06e10192134",
                                                "text": "Some [grammatical writers] call these affections of the verb moods; others call them divisions, qualities, states, species, &c.; and as to the various appellations of each mood we have the personative and impersonative, the indicative, declarative, definitive, modus finiendi, modus fatendi, the rogative, interrogative, requisitive, percontative, assertive, enunciative, vocative, precative, deprecative, responsive, concessive, permissive, promissive, adhortative, optative, dubitative, imperative, mandative, conjunctive, subjunctive, adjunctive, potential, participial, infinitive, and probably many others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b94be622-ad0c-4a38-8691-a7f2c7828f89",
                                                "sense_id": "3b0a5cf0-449d-31c9-9859-f06e10192134",
                                                "text": "‘Perfect Dicibles are of various sorts: Interrogative; Percontative; Adjurative; Optative; Imprecative; Execrative; Substitutive; Compellative; Hypothetical; and, lastly, Dubious.’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2026fe3-f0bc-435a-9e27-3cc4dbda7f24",
                                                "sense_id": "3b0a5cf0-449d-31c9-9859-f06e10192134",
                                                "text": "Destined for internal consumption, these three words nevertheless provoked the reply which you see here: who doesn’t? With an interrogation point, for the reply was percontative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
